  "cues": [
   [
    0.091,
    "A fat is a glycerol head with three fatty acid tails."
   ],
   [
    3.984,
    "Digestion cuts them apart."
   ],
   [
    5.964,
    "Glycerol is a small three-carbon piece, and it enters glycolysis at glyceraldehyde three phosphate."
   ],
   [
    13.112,
    "The long fatty acid tails go through beta oxidation, which snips them two carbons at a time into acetyl co-A, ready for the citric acid cycle."
   ],
   [
    22.839,
    "Those tails are packed with energy."
   ],
   [
    24.896,
    "An oxidized gram of fat produces more than twice as much A T P as an oxidized gram of carbohydrate."
   ],
   [
    32.24,
    "A rough guide, not from the slides: about nine kilocalories per gram for fat, and about four for carbohydrate."
   ],
   [
    39.922,
    "That is why a body stores its long-term energy as fat."
   ],
   [
    43.529,
