  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "The junction works in both directions."
   ],
   [
    2.591,
    "The body also has to build things: amino acids, fats, sugars, the parts of its own cells."
   ],
   [
    9.596,
    "This is biosynthesis, the anabolic pathways."
   ],
   [
    13.099,
    "They draw their small molecules straight from food, or from glycolysis, or from the citric acid cycle."
   ],
   [
    19.844,
    "So a molecule in the cycle can be burned for A T P, or pulled out and built into something new."
   ],
   [
    26.224,
    "Breaking down and building up share the same crossroads."
   ],
   [
    29.896,
    "That is why the cell must keep deciding which way the traffic goes."
   ]
  ]
 },
