   [
    0.117,
    "Who decides?"
   ],
   [
    1.224,
    "Not a manager, but feedback."
   ],
   [
    3.346,
    "If A T P begins to run low, respiration speeds up."
   ],
   [
    7.578,
    "If there is plenty of A T P, respiration slows down."
   ],
   [
    11.641,
    "The cell does this mainly by regulating the activity of enzymes at strategic points in the pathway."
   ],
   [
    17.721,
    "You met the idea in chapter eight, lesson eight."
   ],
   [
    20.99,
    "Feedback inhibition is when an end product switches off its own pathway, as isoleucine switched off enzyme one."
   ],
   [
    28.398,
    "Here the end product is A T P, and the pathway is the whole respiration map."
   ],
   [
    33.971,
    "The strategic point is an enzyme called phosphofructokinase, at the third step of glycolysis."
   ],
   [
    40.312,
    "It turns fructose six phosphate into fructose one, six bisphosphate, which commits the sugar to being split."
   ],
   [
    47.969,
    "It is the main valve of the map."
   ]
